    <h2>How does SynthID Audio work? Short-Time Fourier Transform mathematical embedding</h2>
    <p>
      SynthID Audio operates in the frequency-time spectrogram domain using the Short-Time Fourier Transform (STFT). During the audio generation process, continuous audio samples $x(t)$ are windowed and converted into complex spectral coefficients $X(m, k)$, where $m$ is the time frame index and $k$ represents discrete frequency bins.
    </p>
    <p>
      The embedding model modulates the spectral magnitude $|X(m, k)|$ while strictly respecting the psychoacoustic masking threshold $\Theta(m, k)$, below which human ears cannot distinguish acoustic variations:
    </p>
    <div class="math-box">
      <code>|X'(m, k)| = |X(m, k)| + &alpha; &middot; P(m, k) &middot; &Theta;(m, k)</code>
    </div>
    <p>
      Here, <code>&alpha;</code> is the watermark scaling factor (typically calibrated between 0.008 and 0.015), <code>P(m, k)</code> is a pseudo-random acoustic key sequence generated by DeepMind's model, and <code>&Theta;(m, k)</code> ensures that the added perturbation energy remains at least 15 dB below the masking curve established by dominant harmonic tones.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Worked Example with Real Numbers:</strong> Consider an audio frame featuring a 1 kHz vocal fundamental tone that creates a psychoacoustic masking threshold of <code>-38 dB</code> (amplitude 0.0126) at the adjacent <code>f = 1250 Hz</code> frequency bin. If the baseline spectral magnitude is <code>|X| = 0.0450</code>, the pseudo-random key value is <code>P = +1.0</code>, and <code>&alpha; = 0.012</code>, the resulting modulated magnitude is:
    </p>
    <div class="math-box">
      <code>|X'| = 0.0450 + (0.012 &middot; 1.0 &middot; 0.0126) = 0.0450 + 0.000151 = 0.045151</code>
    </div>
    <p>
      Because the delta of 0.000151 units lies completely below human hearing thresholds, listeners hear a perfectly clean, natural track. However, when Google's neural detector aggregates the phase and magnitude alignment across hundreds of sequential STFT windows, the cumulative correlation exceeds the threshold <code>&tau; = 0.80</code>, confirming the track as AI generated.
    </p>

